-- #822: the IMPORT-ORDER twin of graded_iface_head_collision_modules.  Same two
-- modules, same two graded interfaces spelling their head `f` with the Row in
-- different slots — the ONLY difference from its sibling is that these two import
-- lines are swapped.
--
-- A symmetric single-file fixture cannot see this class of bug and is what hid it the
-- first time: with a program-global bare-name key, whichever module compiled first
-- kept the entry, so swapping these two lines flipped WHICH interface was rejected
-- (`GB` in one order, `GA` in the other — both reproduced on the pre-fix compiler).
-- The pair must now agree, and agree with the clean answer.
import gb.{GB, gb}
import ga.{GA, ga}

export both : Int
both = 1
